      "settlementKey": "iazethas:Pokbith",
      "description": "Barney Rook is a cranky Hederan retired marksman who has turned the Pokbith Archive into a half-library, half-firing nest, and he insists both functions are equally educational. Age has not softened his eye or his temper; he still names favored weapons, lectures strangers about sightlines, and treats every broken turret like a neglected old soldier. The Brass Concordat keeps him close because he knows how old defenses fail, how monsters breach them, and which official records lied about both.",
      "settlementAndAncestryTexture": "Pokbith is a Village in Iazethas, under Triumvirate, with low danger, Partial forest, Farming, Mountain range terrain. Local records favor Altruistic, Lawful, Cooperative, Honorable civic habits; common communities include Human, Halfling — Lightfoot Halfling, Halfling — Stout Halfling, Kender, Kithkin. Hederan reads through the Hederan entry of the race compendium, within Primitive, Tribal, and Wilderness Humanoids, marked by Asethyr. Wilderness-bound survivalists adapted to harsh biomes through ritualized instinct and ancestral knowledge. They thrive in isolation but maintain strong clan bonds. Table cues: Darkvision, Outdoor Adept, Protected by Nature, Friend of Fauna; starting tendency Neutral - Chaotic - Neutral - Honorable.",
      "rumors": [
        "Barney Rook knows why an ichor ledger changed hands last Ishtaday.",
        "Barney Rook has a contact in Velkynwood who will deny everything."
      ],
      "plotHooks": [
